:HELP NAME=ADDTAPCTG.Add Tape Cartridge (ADDTAPCTG)
:P.Use the Add Tape Cartridge (ADDTAPCTG) command to move cartridges of
a media library out of *INSERT into a usable category.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTAPCTG/DEV'.Library device (DEV)
:P.The library device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTAPCTG/CTG'.Cartridge ID (CTG)
:P.The cartridge identifier, as on the cartridge's label.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 40 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *INSERT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTAPCTG/CGY'.Category (CGY)
:P.The category of the volume in the media library.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Category name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHARE400, *NOSHARE, *CNV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Category system
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDTAPCTG/CHECK'.Check volume identifier (CHECK)
:P.Whether to check volume identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=APYPTF.Apply PTF (APYPTF)
:P.Use the Apply PTF (APYPTF) command to apply loaded program temporary
fixes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/SELECT'.PTF numbers to select (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers to select for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/OMIT'.PTF numbers to omit (OMIT)
:P.The PTF numbers to omit for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/APY'.Extent of change (APY)
:P.The extent of change for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TEMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/DELAYED'.Delayed PTFs (DELAYED)
:P.Whether to delayed PTFs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/IPLAPY'.Apply at unattended IPL (IPLAPY)
:P.Whether to apply at unattended IPL.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='APYPTF/APYREQ'.Apply requisite PTFs (APYREQ)
:P.Whether to apply requisite PTFs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSYSVAL.Change System Value (CHGSYSVAL)
:P.Use the Change System Value (CHGSYSVAL) command to change a system
value.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSYSVAL/SYSVAL'.System value (SYSVAL)
:P.The system value.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value must be one of the values F4 lists.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSYSVAL/VALUE'.New value (VALUE)
:P.The new value for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTAPCTG.Change Tape Cartridge (CHGTAPCTG)
:P.Use the Change Tape Cartridge (CHGTAPCTG) command to move cartridges
of a media library to another category.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPCTG/DEV'.Library device (DEV)
:P.The library device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPCTG/CTG'.Cartridge ID (CTG)
:P.The cartridge identifier, as on the cartridge's label.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 40 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPCTG/CGY'.Category (CGY)
:P.The category of the volume in the media library.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Category name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHARE400, *NOSHARE, *CNV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Category system
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGTAPF.Change Tape File (CHGTAPF)
:P.Use the Change Tape File (CHGTAPF) command to change the attributes
of a tape file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/DEV'.Tape device (DEV)
:P.The tape device for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/REELS'.Tape reels (REELS)
:P.The tape reels for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/LABEL'.Tape label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/RCDLEN'.Record length (RCDLEN)
:P.The length of the records, in bytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/BLKLEN'.Block length (BLKLEN)
:P.The block length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 262144.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/RCDBLKTYP'.Record block type (RCDBLKTYP)
:P.The record block type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *F, *FB, *V, *VB, *U.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/CODE'.Code (CODE)
:P.The code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EBCDIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/ENDOPT'.End of tape option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGTAPF/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKTAP.Check Tape (CHKTAP)
:P.Use the Check Tape (CHKTAP) command to check the volume or file on a
tape device.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PK.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/CRTDATE'.Creation date (CRTDATE)
:P.The date and time the spooled file was created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKTAP/ENDOPT'.End of tape option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYFRMTAP.Copy From Tape (CPYFRMTAP)
:P.Use the Copy From Tape (CPYFRMTAP) command to copy the records of a
tape file to a database member or to a listing.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMFILE'.Tape file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/TOFILE'.To file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed&colon. it goes to a spooled file of the job.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMSEQNBR'.Sequence number (FROMSEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMLABEL'.Tape label (FROMLABEL)
:P.The tape label for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/TOMBR'.Member (TOMBR)
:P.The member of the to-file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMLABEL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMDEV'.Device (FROMDEV)
:P.The device the data comes from.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMREELS'.Copy from reels (FROMREELS)
:P.The copy from reels for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Label processing type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SL.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Number of reels
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMRCDLEN'.Record length (FROMRCDLEN)
:P.The record length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMENDOPT'.End of tape option (FROMENDOPT)
:P.The end of tape option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound to its start when the operation ends.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/MBROPT'.Replace or add records (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/OUTFMT'.Print format (OUTFMT)
:P.The format of the output.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHAR:EPK.
:PD.Character.
:PT.:PK.*HEX:EPK.
:PD.Hexadecimal&colon. the characters are compared by their code values,
and no conversion is done.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMVOL'.Volume identifier (FROMVOL)
:P.The volume identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMBLKLEN'.Block length (FROMBLKLEN)
:P.The block length for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 262144.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/FROMRCDBLK'.Record block type (FROMRCDBLK)
:P.The record block type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *F, *FB, *V, *VB, *U.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYFRMTAP/NBRRCDS'.Number of records to copy (NBRRCDS)
:P.The number of records to copy for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYPTF.Copy PTF (CPYPTF)
:P.Use the Copy PTF (CPYPTF) command to copy PTF save files to a save
file or a device.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/SELECT'.PTF numbers to select (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers to select for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/TODEV'.To device (TODEV)
:P.The device the data goes to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/FROMDEV'.From device (FROMDEV)
:P.The device the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/TOSAVF'.To save file (TOSAVF)
:P.The to save file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PTFID:EPK.
:PD.The PTF identifier.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PTFID:EPK.
:PD.The PTF identifier.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QGPL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/TOSEQNBR'.To sequence number (TOSEQNBR)
:P.The to sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/TOENDOPT'.To device end option (TOENDOPT)
:P.What the to-device does with the tape when the operation ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound to its start when the operation ends.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/CPYPTFCVR'.Copy PTF cover letter (CPYPTFCVR)
:P.Whether to copy PTF cover letter.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYPTF/REPLACE'.Replace save file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CPYTOTAP.Copy To Tape (CPYTOTAP)
:P.Use the Copy To Tape (CPYTOTAP) command to copy the records of a
database member to a tape file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/FROMFILE'.From file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOFILE'.Tape file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/FROMMBR'.From member (FROMMBR)
:P.The member the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOSEQNBR'.File sequence number (TOSEQNBR)
:P.The file sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOLABEL'.Tape label (TOLABEL)
:P.The tape label for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMMBR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TODEV'.Device (TODEV)
:P.The device the data goes to.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOREELS'.Copy to reels (TOREELS)
:P.The copy to reels for this command.
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Label processing type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TORCDLEN'.Record length (TORCDLEN)
:P.The record length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOENDOPT'.End of tape option (TOENDOPT)
:P.What the to-device does with the tape when the operation ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound to its start when the operation ends.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOVOL'.Volume identifier (TOVOL)
:P.The volume identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOBLKLEN'.Block length (TOBLKLEN)
:P.The block length for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 262144.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TORCDBLK'.Record block type (TORCDBLK)
:P.The record block type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *F, *FB, *V, *VB, *U.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/TOEXPDATE'.File expiration date (TOEXPDATE)
:P.The file expiration date for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/NBRRCDS'.Number of records to copy (NBRRCDS)
:P.The number of records to copy for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be greater than 0.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CPYTOTAP/COMPACT'.Data compaction (COMPACT)
:P.Whether the device compacts data as it writes it to the tape.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*TAPF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the tape file.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTTAPF.Create Tape File (CRTTAPF)
:P.Use the Create Tape File (CRTTAPF) command to create a tape file
(*FILE TAPF)&colon. the device, volumes, labels and record layout
CPYTOTAP and CPYFRMTAP take by default.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/DEV'.Tape device (DEV)
:P.The tape device for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/REELS'.Tape reels (REELS)
:P.The tape reels for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 1 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/LABEL'.Tape label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/RCDLEN'.Record length (RCDLEN)
:P.The length of the records, in bytes.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/BLKLEN'.Block length (BLKLEN)
:P.The block length for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 262144.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/RCDBLKTYP'.Record block type (RCDBLKTYP)
:P.The record block type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *F, *FB, *V, *VB, *U.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/CODE'.Code (CODE)
:P.The code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EBCDIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.It never expires.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/ENDOPT'.End of tape option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTTAPF/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPHDWRSC.Display Hardware Resources (DSPHDWRSC)
:P.Use the Display Hardware Resources (DSPHDWRSC) command to show the
hardware resources of one kind.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPHDWRSC/TYPE'.Type (TYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AHW, *CMN, *CRP, *CSA, *LWS, *PRC, *STG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPHDWRSC/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPHDWRSC/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPHDWRSC/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPTF.Display PTF (DSPPTF)
:P.Use the Display PTF (DSPPTF) command to show the program temporary
fixes of a licensed program.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/SELECT'.PTF numbers (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/COVERONLY'.Cover letter only (COVERONLY)
:P.Whether to cover letter only.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTF/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPPTFCVR.Display PTF Cover Letter (DSPPTFCVR)
:P.Use the Display PTF Cover Letter (DSPPTFCVR) command to show the
cover letters of program temporary fixes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTFCVR/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTFCVR/SELECT'.PTF numbers to select (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers to select for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTFCVR/CVRATR'.Cover letter attribute (CVRATR)
:P.The cover letter attribute for this command.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SPCINST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTFCVR/STATUS'.PTF status (STATUS)
:P.The PTF status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOTAPY, *APYPERM, *APYTEMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPPTFCVR/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSFWRSC.Display Software Resources (DSPSFWRSC)
:P.Use the Display Software Resources (DSPSFWRSC) command to show the
installed software resources.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSFWRSC/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSFWRSC/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSFWRSC/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSYSVAL.Display System Value (DSPSYSVAL)
:P.Use the Display System Value (DSPSYSVAL) command to display a system
value.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSYSVAL/SYSVAL'.System value (SYSVAL)
:P.The system value.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value must be one of the values F4 lists.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSYSVAL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPTAP.Display Tape (DSPTAP)
:P.Use the Display Tape (DSPTAP) command to display the labels, or the
saves, on a tape volume.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting file sequence number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending file sequence number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/DATA'.Data type (DATA)
:P.The data type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVRST:EPK.
:PD.Save and restore operations.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LABELS, *VOLLBL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/ENDOPT'.End of tape option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAP/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPTAPCTG.Display Tape Cartridge (DSPTAPCTG)
:P.Use the Display Tape Cartridge (DSPTAPCTG) command to display the
tape cartridges of a media library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/DEV'.Library device (DEV)
:P.The library device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/CTG'.Cartridge ID (CTG)
:P.The cartridge identifier, as on the cartridge's label.
:P.Up to 40 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 6 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/CGY'.Category (CGY)
:P.The category of the volume in the media library.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Category name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:PT.:PK.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHARE400, *NOSHARE, *INSERT, *EJECT, *CNV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Category system
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPTAPCTG/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DUPTAP.Duplicate Tape (DUPTAP)
:P.Use the Duplicate Tape (DUPTAP) command to copy files from the tape
on one device to another.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/FROMDEV'.From device (FROMDEV)
:P.The device the data comes from.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/TODEV'.To device (TODEV)
:P.The device the data goes to.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/FROMSEQNBR'.From sequence number (FROMSEQNBR)
:P.The from sequence number for this command.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Starting file sequence number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Ending file sequence number
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LAST:EPK.
:PD.The last one.
:PT.:PK.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/TOSEQNBR'.To sequence number (TOSEQNBR)
:P.The to sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMSEQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/FROMVOL'.From volume identifier (FROMVOL)
:P.The from volume identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/TOVOL'.To volume identifier (TOVOL)
:P.The to volume identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/TODENSITY'.Tape density (TODENSITY)
:P.The tape density for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DEVTYPE, *CTGTYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/COMPACT'.Data compaction (COMPACT)
:P.Whether the device compacts data as it writes it to the tape.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/FILES'.Files to duplicate (FILES)
:P.The files to duplicate for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ACTIVE:EPK.
:PD.Active.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/USRLBLPGM'.User label program (USRLBLPGM)
:P.The user label program for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYSCOPY.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/FROMENDOPT'.From device end option (FROMENDOPT)
:P.The from device end option for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound to its start when the operation ends.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/TOENDOPT'.To device end option (TOENDOPT)
:P.What the to-device does with the tape when the operation ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound to its start when the operation ends.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK DEF.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/CHECK'.Check for active files (CHECK)
:P.Whether to check for active files.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPTAP/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=GO.Go to Menu (GO)
:P.Use the Go to Menu (GO) command to show a menu.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='GO/MENU'.Menu (MENU)
:P.The menu for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='GO/RTNPNT'.Return point (RTNPNT)
:P.Whether to return point.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=INSPTF.Install PTF (INSPTF)
:P.Use the Install PTF (INSPTF) command to load and apply every PTF of a
package in requisite order, now or at the next IPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/INSTYPE'.Install type (INSTYPE)
:P.The install type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DLYALL, *DLYIPL, *IMMDLY, *IMMONLY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/PTFTYPE'.PTF type (PTFTYPE)
:P.The PTF type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLPTF, *HIPERLIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/OMIT'.PTF numbers to omit (OMIT)
:P.The PTF numbers to omit for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSPTF/PTFGRP'.PTF group (PTFGRP)
:P.The PTF group for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 60 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=INZTAP.Initialize Tape (INZTAP)
:P.Use the Initialize Tape (INZTAP) command to initialize the tape on a
device, labeled or not.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/NEWVOL'.New volume identifier (NEWVOL)
:P.The new volume identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CTGID.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/NEWOWNID'.New owner identifier (NEWOWNID)
:P.The new owner identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.Blanks&colon. no value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 14 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/CHECK'.Check for active files (CHECK)
:P.The check for active files for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/DENSITY'.Tape density (DENSITY)
:P.The tape density for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DEVTYPE, *CTGTYPE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/CODE'.Code (CODE)
:P.The code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ASCII:EPK.
:PD.ASCII.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *EBCDIC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/ENDOPT'.End of tape option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZTAP/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.Whether to clear.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LODPTF.Load PTF (LODPTF)
:P.Use the Load PTF (LODPTF) command to load program temporary fixes
from save files or media.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/SELECT'.PTF numbers to select (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers to select for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/OMIT'.PTF numbers to omit (OMIT)
:P.The PTF numbers to omit for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/SPRPTF'.Superseded PTFs (SPRPTF)
:P.The superseded PTFs for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *APYPERM, *NOAPY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/COVER'.Cover letter file (COVER)
:P.The cover letter file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODPTF/PATHID'.Path identifier (PATHID)
:P.The path identifier for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 9999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCHGUPDA.Change Update Attributes (QSCHGUPDA)
:P.Use the Change Update Attributes (QSCHGUPDA) command to where the
update service is and when to check it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGUPDA/URL'.Update service URL (URL)
:P.The update service URL for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGUPDA/PROXY'.Proxy host and port (PROXY)
:P.The proxy host and port for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGUPDA/SCHEDULE'.Check for updates (SCHEDULE)
:P.When the spooled file can begin to print&colon. as soon as it is
created, when it is closed, or when the job ends.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*WEEKLY:EPK.
:PD.Weekly.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DAILY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGUPDA/SCDTIME'.Time of the check (SCDTIME)
:P.The time the job is scheduled to run.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCHKUPD.Check for Updates (QSCHKUPD)
:P.Use the Check for Updates (QSCHKUPD) command to ask the update
service what is newer than this system has.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCRTPTF.Create PTF from Manifest (QSCRTPTF)
:P.Use the Create PTF from Manifest (QSCRTPTF) command to build a signed
PTF save file from a manifest in the IFS&colon. the header, the objects
on this system, a cover letter.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTPTF/MANIFEST'.Manifest stream file (MANIFEST)
:P.The manifest stream file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTPTF/KEYFILE'.Signing key file (KEYFILE)
:P.The signing key file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTPTF/TOSAVF'.To save file (TOSAVF)
:P.The to save file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PTFID:EPK.
:PD.The PTF identifier.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PTFID:EPK.
:PD.The PTF identifier.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QGPL is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTPTF/REPLACE'.Replace save file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSGROWIFS.Grow the IFS (QSGROWIFS)
:P.Use the Grow the IFS (QSGROWIFS) command to give the integrated file
system more of ASP 1 now.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSGROWIFS/SIZE'.Storage to add (MB) (SIZE)
:P.The storage to add (MB) for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 64 to 16777216.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STEP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSHWQUAL.Qualify Hardware (QSHWQUAL)
:P.Use the Qualify Hardware (QSHWQUAL) command to check this machine's
hardware for QS/400 and grade each resource pass, warn or fail; shown,
printed, or also written to a FAT USB stick.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSHWQUAL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSHWQUAL/TODEV'.Also write to device (TODEV)
:P.The device the data goes to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVPTF.Remove PTF (RMVPTF)
:P.Use the Remove PTF (RMVPTF) command to remove program temporary
fixes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, 5770SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/SELECT'.PTF numbers to select (SELECT)
:P.The PTF numbers to select for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/OMIT'.PTF numbers to omit (OMIT)
:P.The PTF numbers to omit for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/RMV'.Extent of change (RMV)
:P.The extent of change for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TEMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/DELAYED'.Delayed PTFs (DELAYED)
:P.Whether to delayed PTFs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/IPLRMV'.Remove at unattended IPL (IPLRMV)
:P.Whether to remove at unattended IPL.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVPTF/RMVDEP'.Remove dependent PTFs (RMVDEP)
:P.Whether to remove dependent PTFs.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVTAPCTG.Remove Tape Cartridge (RMVTAPCTG)
:P.Use the Remove Tape Cartridge (RMVTAPCTG) command to eject cartridges
from a media library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTAPCTG/DEV'.Library device (DEV)
:P.The library device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTAPCTG/CTG'.Cartridge ID (CTG)
:P.The cartridge identifier, as on the cartridge's label.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 40 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVTAPCTG/STATION'.Station (STATION)
:P.The station for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CNV, *BULK.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SNDPTFORD.Send PTF Order (SNDPTFORD)
:P.Use the Send PTF Order (SNDPTFORD) command to order PTFs, groups or a
cumulative package from the update service; they arrive as save files in
QGPL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/PTFID'.PTF description (PTFID)
:P.The PTF description for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. PTF identifier
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 9 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Product
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONLYPRD.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Release
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ONLYRLS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/PTFPART'.PTF parts (PTFPART)
:P.The PTF parts for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CVRLTR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/RMTCPNAME'.Remote control point (RMTCPNAME)
:P.The remote control point for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IBMSRV, *SELECT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/DLVRYFMT'.Delivery format (DLVRYFMT)
:P.The delivery format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IMAGE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/ORDER'.Order (ORDER)
:P.The order for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PTFID:EPK.
:PD.The PTF identifier.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *REQUIRED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/REORDER'.Reorder (REORDER)
:P.Whether to reorder.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/CHKPTF'.Check PTF (CHKPTF)
:P.Whether to check PTF.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SNDPTFORD/IMGDIR'.Image directory (IMGDIR)
:P.The image directory for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRSST.Start System Service Tools (STRSST)
:P.Use the Start System Service Tools (STRSST) command to start the
system service tools; the service tools sign-on is a screen, so the
command has no parameters.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKHDWRSC.Work with Hardware Resources (WRKHDWRSC)
:P.Use the Work with Hardware Resources (WRKHDWRSC) command to list the
hardware resources of one kind and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKHDWRSC/TYPE'.Type (TYPE)
:P.The type for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CMN, *CRP, *CSA, *LWS, *PRC, *STG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKMLBSTS.Work with Media Library Status (WRKMLBSTS)
:P.Use the Work with Media Library Status (WRKMLBSTS) command to work
with media libraries and their drives.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKMLBSTS/MLB'.Media library (MLB)
:P.The media library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKPTFGRP.Work with PTF Groups (WRKPTFGRP)
:P.The Work with PTF Groups (WRKPTFGRP) command works with the PTF
groups on the system, their levels and status.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPTFGRP/PTFGRP'.PTF group (PTFGRP)
:P.The PTF group for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 60 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKPTFGRP/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSYSVAL.Work with System Values (WRKSYSVAL)
:P.Use the Work with System Values (WRKSYSVAL) command to work with the
system values, all or one group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSVAL/SYSVAL'.System value (SYSVAL)
:P.The system value.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*MSG:EPK.
:PD.A message is sent.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALC, *DATTIM, *EDT, *SEC, *STG, *SYSCTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSYSVAL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKTAPCTG.Work with Tape Cartridges (WRKTAPCTG)
:P.Use the Work with Tape Cartridges (WRKTAPCTG) command to work with
the tape cartridges of a media library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTAPCTG/DEV'.Library device (DEV)
:P.The library device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTAPCTG/CTG'.Cartridge ID (CTG)
:P.The cartridge identifier, as on the cartridge's label.
:P.Up to 40 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 6 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKTAPCTG/CGY'.Category (CGY)
:P.The category of the volume in the media library.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Category name
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*IPL:EPK.
:PD.During the IPL.
:PT.:PK.*NL:EPK.
:PD.Not less than.
:PT.:PK.*SYSGEN:EPK.
:PD.The value the system generates.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SHARE400, *NOSHARE, *INSERT, *EJECT, *CNV.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Category system
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
